# Xcode build artifacts
Build/
build/
DerivedData/

# User-specific Xcode data
*.xcuserdata/
xcuserdata/

# macOS metadata
.DS_Store

# TextureLoader's decoded-texture cache (see TextureLoader.swift): raw RGBA next to each source
# image, regenerated on demand and invalidated by mtime. It is ~2x the PNG it came from and the
# MegaKit's alone is 165 MB — it nearly tripled the asset slice below before this line existed.
.rgba-cache/

# Large unused model kit (~164 MB of PBR textures) — held out of plain git pending a
# git-LFS decision. Only needed when the fort multi-texture feature is built (M12); it is
# loaded from this local path at runtime in the meantime.
Mazen_Models/modular_fort_01_2k/

# Quaternius Ultimate Stylized Nature Pack — heavy, multi-format (36 MB .blend + FBX + glTF
# duplicates we don't use). Loaded locally from OBJ/ + Textures/ at runtime, like WenrexaTrees.
Mazen_Models/Quaternius Ultimate Stylized Nature Pack/

# In-use imported asset packs — the LOADED SLICE IS TRACKED, the rest is not.
#
# AssetRegistry reads exactly two things from each pack: `OBJ/` and (for the textured ones) the
# pack's texture folder. Everything else in these directories is source material we never open —
# .blend files, FBX/glTF duplicates, engine-project .zips, preview renders — and that, not the
# models, is what made them 515 MB. Tracking only what the loader reads costs ~85 MB and means a
# fresh clone RUNS: the galleries are whole, the garden is planted, Scene 6's underside is dressed.
#
# The paths are unchanged, so no loader change was needed — git simply stops carrying the ballast.
# Adding a pack? Follow the same shape, and check `AssetRegistry.loadAll` for which folders it
# actually reads before deciding what to un-ignore.
Mazen_Models/Dungeons Pack/*
!Mazen_Models/Dungeons Pack/OBJ/
!Mazen_Models/Dungeons Pack/License.txt
Mazen_Models/Nature Pack/*
!Mazen_Models/Nature Pack/OBJ/
!Mazen_Models/Nature Pack/License.txt
Mazen_Models/Ruins Pack/*
!Mazen_Models/Ruins Pack/OBJ/
!Mazen_Models/Ruins Pack/Textures/
!Mazen_Models/Ruins Pack/License.txt
Mazen_Models/Cyberpunk Pack/*
!Mazen_Models/Cyberpunk Pack/OBJ/
!Mazen_Models/Cyberpunk Pack/Textures/
!Mazen_Models/Cyberpunk Pack/License.txt

# MegaKit, same rule with one extra cut: the loader resolves 18 diffuse maps out of
# `Blends/textures`, and never a normal map. The `*_Normal.png` files are 26 MB of the folder's
# 53 MB and nothing reads them — if a normal-map path is ever built, un-ignore them then.
Mazen_Models/Stylized Nature MegaKit/*
!Mazen_Models/Stylized Nature MegaKit/OBJ/
!Mazen_Models/Stylized Nature MegaKit/License_Source.txt
!Mazen_Models/Stylized Nature MegaKit/Blends/
Mazen_Models/Stylized Nature MegaKit/Blends/*
!Mazen_Models/Stylized Nature MegaKit/Blends/textures/
Mazen_Models/Stylized Nature MegaKit/Blends/textures/*_Normal.png

# Blocks Pack (Quaternius CubeWorldKit) — same rule. It shipped with NO license file, unlike the
# five packs above, which held up committing it: an asset in git is an asset REDISTRIBUTED, and
# history is permanent. Eddie identified the source — quaternius.com/packs/cubeworldkit.html —
# putting it with the same author as every other pack here; provenance is recorded in
# `Blocks Pack/PROVENANCE.md` since the download itself carries nothing.
Mazen_Models/Blocks Pack/*
!Mazen_Models/Blocks Pack/OBJ/
!Mazen_Models/Blocks Pack/Textures/
!Mazen_Models/Blocks Pack/PROVENANCE.md
